NOTE         | img_root_moved     | 2026-08-28 (same day, second move) - relocated one level deeper, from `NNEST-11.17/rmmv-www-img` directly to `NNEST-11.17/#.NNEST_ASSETS/rmmv-www-img`, per direct instruction: `#.NNEST_ASSETS` is meant to be a general asset container at the zip-parent level so OTHER future asset types (not just RMMV) can live as siblings under it, not just this one RMMV-specific folder. `rmmv-www-img` keeps its own name as a subfolder of that general container - nothing about the RMMV-specific layout inside it changed, only its parent.
NOTE         | img_root_why       | Real, stable LOCAL copy of the game's www/img tree, used by palettes_manager.c's rmmv-img-dir tabs (tilesets + characters/faces/battlebacks/etc). Deliberately NOT inside `yz.muchiverse/44.xyz.../&.widgits/palettes/` (that folder gets zipped/shared as "the house" and was accumulating real PNG bloat - see RMMV-IMG-DIR-TABS-PLAN.md §10). img_root instead lives one level above the house, at the NNEST-11.17 zip-parent level, still local disk, still stable across sessions, just outside what gets bundled. This is the ONLY path the C manager (palettes_manager.c's rmmv_img_root()/rmmv_resolve_img_dir()) reads for these tabs now - no hardcoded `&.widgits/palettes/assets/` or `/media/.../www/img` fallback after the 2026-08-28 refactor. mount_point/project_root above stay as historical reference to where these files were SOURCED from (the real deployed game on the USB drive) - img_root is where the house's own copy now permanently lives, independent of whether that drive is mounted.
